Variance vs. Precision Trade-Off: A single Decision Tree achieves high recall (84.52%) but suffers from severe fold-to-fold instability (± 4.50% precision SD) and over-flags safe borrowers (41.01% precision). Shallow Gradient Boosting (max_depth=5, 80 stages) underfits high-cardinality categorical splits (0.3980 F1) while requiring the longest runtime.

Why Random Forest Was Selected: By aggregating 100 deep decorrelated trees (max_depth=22, class_weight='balanced_subsample'), Random Forest cuts cross-validation F1 variance by 93% (±0.0029) and boosts precision by +14.61 percentage points over
the Decision Tree while preserving strong default capture (76.79% recall). On the untouched 50,400-row test set, the final serialized model (credit_risk_rf_artifact.joblib) achieves 89.30% Accuracy, 54.62% Precision, 76.85% Recall, 0.6386 F1-Score, 
and 0.9306 ROC-AUC—correctly identifying 4,764 of 6,199 true defaults (TN = 40,243, FP = 3,958, FN = 1,435), with Income_per_Age (12.0%), Income (12.0%), CITY (11.4%), Exp_to_Age_Ratio (10.2%), and Profession (10.2%) serving as the top predictive drivers.

6. Operational Recommendations
Tiered Underwriting Triage via the Streamlit Decision-Support App: Route applications into three human-review tracks based on predicted default probability rather than binary auto-rejection:

Low Risk (< 30% probability): Fast-track standard KYC and automated income verification.

Moderate / Borderline Risk (30% – 55% probability): Require enhanced verification of payslips, bank statements, and existing debt obligations before approval.

High Risk (≥ 55% probability): Escalate to senior underwriters to evaluate risk-mitigating structures (co-signers, collateral, or reduced principal limits).

Targeted Probation & Liquidity Checks: Institute mandatory employment-confirmation checks for applicants with CURRENT_JOB_YRS < 3 (15.65% segment default rate) and explicit rent-to-income cash-flow reviews for rented housing applicants (12.56% segment default rate).

Portfolio Monitoring & Quarterly Recalibration: Track realized default rates against predicted risk tiers quarterly and retrain the Joblib pipeline whenever regional macroeconomic shifts or occupational default rates drift by more than ±2.0 percentage points.

7. Limitations & Governance Considerations
Absence of Credit Bureau & Debt-Obligation Variables: The dataset lacks external credit scores, existing debt-to-income (DTI) ratios, requested loan size, and interest rate terms. Consequently, 45.38% of applicants flagged at the 0.50 cutoff (3,958 of 8,722 test flags) are false positives who did not default—reinforcing why human adjudication of external credit bureau files is mandatory before declining any applicant.

Repeated Cohort Structure: Because the 252,000 rows map to 42,007 unique demographic/occupational profiles, predictions for brand-new city-profession combinations unseen during training rely on ordinal fallback encoding (-1) and should automatically trigger manual underwriter review.

Fair-Lending & Proxy Governance: High model reliance on CITY, STATE, and Age can act as indirect proxies for protected socioeconomic groups. Periodic disparate-impact audits must be conducted across geographic and demographic segments to ensure equitable credit access.
